      "id": "2tipr3f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Chemical Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chemical reactions transform reactants into products by breaking and making bonds.",
        "A balanced chemical equation strictly obeys the Law of Conservation of Mass.",
        "Key indicators of chemical changes include gas evolution, color change, temperature change, and precipitate formation.",
        "Oxidation is the gain of oxygen or loss of electrons, while reduction is the loss of oxygen or gain of electrons.",
        "Corrosion damages metals via ambient oxidation, whereas rancidity causes foul odor and taste in oxidized fats and oils."
      ],
      "id": "nt0l5cs"
    },
